rborepo-template/commits/f47e77c44f84990bab2944b9a07ec24ab7dcd0ad"}],"sha":"1027830f1ebac0b7d50e383287797beaa6ef8351","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andrewdyer/react-vite-turborepo-template/commits/1027830f1ebac0b7d50e383287797beaa6ef8351"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8114523?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/andrewdyer","id":8114523,"login":"andrewdyer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTQ1MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andrewdyer/react-vite-turborepo-template/commits/f47e77c44f84990bab2944b9a07ec24ab7dcd0ad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T11:07:29Z","email":"andrewdyer@outlook.com","name":"Andrew Dyer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T11:07:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: replace shared workflows (#38)\n\n* ci: update release workflow configuration\n\n* ci: update publish workflow configuration\n\n* ci: update test workflow configuration\n\n* ci: update deploy workflow configuration\n\n* ci: update rollback workflow configuration\n\n* ci: add a typecheck step\n\nAdded a typecheck step to the test workflow\n\n* fix: update e2e script\n\n* ci: update actions to latest major versions\n\nUpdated actions/checkout (v4→v7), actions/setup-node (v4→v7), actions/cache (v4→v6),\npnpm/action-setup (v4→v6), docker/login-action (v3→v4), and googleapis/release-please-action (v4→v5)\nacross all workflow\n\n* ci: add job timeouts\n\nAdded deploy and rollback caps at 15 minutes, publish at 30, and release at 10\n\n* ci: prevent overlapping release-please runs on main\n\nAdd a concurrency group scoped to the main branch ref so two rapid pushes can''t run\nrelease-please in parallel. Overlapping runs would race on the same release PR branch\nand manifest file, and could both attempt to tag/create the same GitHub Release.\ncancel-in-progress is false rather than true (unlike test.yml) since interrupting a\nrelease-please run mid-flight risks leaving a tag, release, or release PR half-updated;\nqueuing behind the in-progress run is safe since it computes changes from full commit\nhistory rather than a diff against the prior run.\n\n* ci: run test workflow on pushes to main, not just pull requests\n\nAdd a push trigger scoped to main alongside the existing pull_request trigger. Merges\nto main previously went untested in two cases: a misconfigured or bypassed branch\nprotection rule, and release-please''s own release PR, which is intentionally skipped\nby the existing release-please-- head ref guard since it only bumps versions and\nchangelogs. This closes both gaps by verifying main''s actual state after every merge,\nindependent of what happened at PR time.\n\nAlso update the concurrency group to fall back to github.ref when\ngithub.event.pull_request.number is unset, since push events don''t have a PR number.\nWithout the fallback every push run would silently share one group (\"test-\"); the\nfallback makes the group key explicit for both trigger types and keeps them from\ncolliding with unrelated PR runs.","tree":{"sha":"d755230f4388bfa4ba6f43490ea390f8bdde9703","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andrewdyer/react-vite-turborepo-template/git/trees/d755230f4388bfa4ba6f43490ea390f8bdde9703"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andrewdyer/react-vite-turborepo-template/git/commits/f47e77c44f84990bab2944b9a07ec24ab7dcd0ad","verification":{"payload":"tree d755230f4388bfa4ba6f43490ea390f8bdde9703\nparent 7e4ebf57d88c959bb80264178bb611ce38723959\nauthor Andrew Dyer <andrewdyer@outlook.com> 1786014449 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786014449 +0100\n\nci: replace shared workflows (#38)\n\n* ci: update release workflow configuration\n\n* ci: update publish workflow configuration\n\n* ci: update test workflow configuration\n\n* ci: update deploy workflow configuration\n\n* ci: update rollback workflow configuration\n\n* ci: add a typecheck step\n\nAdded a typecheck step to the test workflow\n\n* fix: update e2e script\n\n* ci: update actions to latest major versions\n\nUpdated actions/checkout (v4→v7), actions/setup-node (v4→v7), actions/cache (v4→v6),\npnpm/action-setup (v4→v6), docker/login-action (v3→v4), and googleapis/release-please-action (v4→v5)\nacross all workflow\n\n* ci: add job timeouts\n\nAdded deploy and rollback caps at 15 minutes, publish at 30, and release at 10\n\n* ci: prevent overlapping release-please runs on main\n\nAdd a concurrency group scoped to the main branch ref so two rapid pushes can''t run\nrelease-please in parallel. Overlapping runs would race on the same release PR branch\nand manifest file, and could both attempt to tag/create the same GitHub Release.\ncancel-in-progress is false rather than true (unlike test.yml) since interrupting a\nrelease-please run mid-flight risks leaving a tag, release, or release PR half-updated;\nqueuing behind the in-progress run is safe since it computes changes from full commit\nhistory rather than a diff against the prior run.\n\n* ci: run test workflow on pushes to main, not just pull requests\n\nAdd a push trigger scoped to main alongside the existing pull_request trigger. Merges\nto main previously went untested in two cases: a misconfigured or bypassed branch\nprotection rule, and release-please''s own release PR, which is intentionally skipped\nby the existing release-please-- head ref guard since it only bumps versions and\nchangelogs. This closes both gaps by verifying main''s actual state after every merge,\nindependent of what happened at PR time.\n\nAlso update the concurrency group to fall back to github.ref when\ngithub.event.pull_request.number is unset, since push events don''t have a PR number.\nWithout the fallback every push run would silently share one group (\"test-\"); the\nfallback makes the group key explicit for both trigger types and keeps them from\ncolliding with unrelated PR runs.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqdGrxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmXsQABKI5wezEXrysP84dY9/b9HA\n76On/pFtgmhryXAIqUfEd1qU3/o/6RxlPFdOGWDpBbpkFbtyIrkDBmEkMDI5bl7O\nkuoWpf7lqRf6AMUIgAvv2mlEyR9TnJT/xkCybEu1kKN9uqYy015YQL9QuM7ElFrs\nMd6VD+VACNmNG4XrIt6r/bUMzDE36dNllhl1dopxCquYc/YkoYNAlnEoriqu64G9\n1hFDEP4hwhJsgL569f5wcvp1FCwNfo0IrfFk5j7S+fPlAUP6lOykDBc8gPzKCx3r\nW+KExVppHKqX5Jabj38NPZU6PX205/EuErsTLPwevBC83ZZEAhx+I/gKGYXoueda\ntWNdFFuzJWqIei1XCmEkJk9LUPKgAecSJRFBFT/SGtqNUY2Lx8+2PjjwMFiR+R8s\nWUAZ7EtIUxLKF/PMIb4qXOBqKdE3GLfaEh7YabfF3j471EGDcFuMbMcFd8qQlBOT\nLXMfSiIxhe+VCqvttMYb6wDbNahafynC6duZinN+/s4qfW0edx98zeM2bTf2bz6F\nMp/gAgf4oz/1spBziocW1sx7smaaRlEjAZqmD5o72sAuSj0np6K41tI3kxSig4SZ\nbqfdtU70446upCFFet6PpmNaQJw8t8TYpMMhmFEAX66CezOnrb9n5l32lsiFoZGs\nTnytX8tBYwpfUJmlHhnG\n=zuLO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-06T11:53:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id