pi.github.com/repos/andrewdyer/react-vite-turborepo-template/commits/4a81280265343947526e6079e41d1886a018c9b2"}],"sha":"eaed6895ed9c484cc96b80659f65f41b22b5dbb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andrewdyer/react-vite-turborepo-template/commits/eaed6895ed9c484cc96b80659f65f41b22b5dbb0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8114523?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/andrewdyer","id":8114523,"login":"andrewdyer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTQ1MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andrewdyer/react-vite-turborepo-template/commits/4a81280265343947526e6079e41d1886a018c9b2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-01T16:05:24Z","email":"andrewdyer@outlook.com","name":"Andrew Dyer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-01T16:05:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: add CI/CD workflows (#25)\n\n* chore: add publish workflow\n\nAdded publish workflow\n\n* chore: rename workflow\n\nRenamed ci workflow to test for clarity\n\n* chore: add workflow\n\nAdded deloy workflow with placeholder body\n\n* chore: fire deploy event\n\nUpdated the publish workflow to fire a repository dispatch event to trigger the deploy workflow\n\n* ci(test): split workflow into parallel jobs and tighten pnpm setup\n\nReplace the single build-and-test job with three separate jobs — build, test, and e2e — where test and e2e run in parallel once build succeeds. This reduces total CI time and ensures a unit test failure does not block the E2E suite from running concurrently. Also removes the pnpm version: latest pin in favour of the packageManager field in package.json, adds --frozen-lockfile to prevent silent lockfile mutations in CI, and removes the unused fetch-depth: 2 option from the checkout step.\n\n* ci(publish): split npm and docker publishing into parallel jobs\n\nExtract Release Please output retrieval into a dedicated job and run npm package publishing and Docker image building in parallel, both depending on that shared job. This reduces total publish time when both packages and apps are released together, and separates the two concerns so a failure in one does not block the other.\n\n* chore: add workflow\n\nAdded rollback workflow with placeholder body\n\n* docs(deploy): clarify how to enable manual approval via GitHub Environments\n\nThe existing commented-out environment key lacked any explanation of what it does or how to activate it. Replaced the comment with a full description of what uncommenting the line enables and what must be configured in GitHub first.\n\n* docs(deploy): clarify how to enable manual approval via GitHub Environments\n\nThe existing commented-out environment key lacked any explanation of what it does or how to activate it. Replaced the comment with a full description of what uncommenting the line enables and what must be configured in GitHub first.\n\n* docs(setup): rewrite setup documentation\n\nRewrote setup.md from scratch to cover the full repository configuration required before the release chain is operational. The previous version covered only the GitHub Actions workflow permissions and personal access token for Release Please. The new version adds secrets for npm and Docker Hub publishing, branch protection rules for enforcing the Test workflow as a required status check on main, a table of contents, and consistent section introductions throughout.\n\n* docs: add privately-publishing guide for GitHub Packages and GHCR\n\nDocuments how to switch the Publish workflow from the default public targets — npmjs.com and Docker Hub — to GitHub-hosted alternatives. Covers the package.json changes required for GitHub Packages, including scoped naming and publishConfig, and the workflow changes required for both GitHub Packages and the GitHub Container Registry.\n\n* chore: format\n\n* ci: merge workflows\n\nMerged release + publish + deploy into one workflow\n\n* chore: migrate docs\n\nMigrated docs to docs site\n\n* ci: update rollback workflow\n\nUpdated rollback workflow placeholder body\n\n* ci: add timeout\n\nAdded timeout to build and test jobs\n\n* fix: collapse test workflow into single job\n\n* feat: split workflows\n\nSplit release, publish and deploy into standalone workflows\n\n* fix: configure release-please tag format\n\nConfigured release-please tag format to use component prefix\n\n* chore: add packages/shared to release-please config and manifest\n\n* docs: add publishing guidance to shared package readme\n\n* feat: update rollback workflow\n\nUpdated rollback workflow with run-name and ghcr image\n\n* chore: remove changelog\n\nThe release workflow manages changelogs automatically at the package and app level, so the manual changelog tip is redundant and potentially confusing.\n\n* docs: update tooling\n\nUpdated tooling seciton to cover workflows\n\n* chore: remove docs\n\nRemoved redundant docs\n\n* chore: add .npmrc\n\nAdded .npmrc for GitHub Packages registry support\n\n* ci: add action\n\nAdded a reusable action\n\n* ci: update workflow\n\n* ci: add space between steps\n\nAdded space between steps for improved readability\n\n* chore: updated .npmrc\n\nUpdated .npmrc for improved docs on how to use\n\n* chore: support optional authentication\n\nUpdate the pnpm install step in the Dockerfile to optionally mount an npm_token build secret and append the auth token to .npmrc before installing dependencies. If no secret is provided, install proceeds without authentication and only public packages are resolved. The .npmrc file is removed immediately after install in the same RUN instruction so no credentials are stored in any image layer.\n\n* chore: updated .npmrc\n\nUpdated .npmrc so it reads more naturally with registry first and auth docs second\n\n* chore: add env var\n\nAdded NODE_AUTH_TOKEN in the environment for Docker image builds and update comments for clarity.\n\n* chore: update pnpm install action description and inputs\n\nRefine action description and add optional inputs for registry URL and scope.\n\n* chore: update default registry-url in pnpm install action\n\nSet default registry-url to an empty string for flexibility.\n\n* chore: update .npmrc comments for clarity\n\nClarify instructions for configuring GitHub Packages in .npmrc.\n\n* chore: update deployment image reference in workflows\n\nChange GHCR image name example to use a generic organization format.\n\n* chore: update npm install command in Dockerfile\n\nRefine npm install command to improve clarity and maintain security during build.\n\n* chore: update pnpm install action in workflows\n\nAdd registry-url and scope parameters for GitHub Packages.\n\n* chore: update default node version in pnpm install action\n\nSet the default node version to ''22.20.0'' for consistency.\n\n* chore: update comments for clarity in publish workflow\n\nImprove comments in publish.yml for better understanding of tag processing and Docker image building.\n\n* chore: update publish workflow\n\nEnhance comments and error handling in the publish workflow for better maintainability and debugging.\n\n* chore: update comments for clarity in publish workflow\n\nEnhance comments in publish.yml for better understanding of workflow logic.\n\n* chore: :sparkles: update deployment and rollback workflows\n\nAdd validation for deployment and rollback inputs, and provide template instructions for configuration.\n\n* docs: update GitHub Actions CI/CD description\n\nClarify the role of deploy/rollback workflow templates in the README.","tree":{"sha":"8adf3733da0fc37d477ce2c597cb28773515b0c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andrewdyer/react-vite-turborepo-template/git/trees/8adf3733da0fc37d477ce2c597cb28773515b0c6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andrewdyer/react-vite-turborepo-template/git/commits/4a81280265343947526e6079e41d1886a018c9b2","verification":{"payload":"tree 8adf3733da0fc37d477ce2c597cb28773515b0c6\nparent 769de88cb2cff993fd7699325f83c28c137ee953\nauthor Andrew Dyer <andrewdyer@outlook.com> 1782921924 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782921924 +0100\n\nci: add CI/CD workflows (#25)\n\n* chore: add publish workflow\n\nAdded publish workflow\n\n* chore: rename workflow\n\nRenamed ci workflow to test for clarity\n\n* chore: add workflow\n\nAdded deloy workflow with placeholder body\n\n* chore: fire deploy event\n\nUpdated the publish workflow to fire a repository dispatch event to trigger the deploy workflow\n\n* ci(test): split workflow into parallel jobs and tighten pnpm setup\n\nReplace the single build-and-test job with three separate jobs — build, test, and e2e — where test and e2e run in parallel once build succeeds. This reduces total CI time and ensures a unit test failure does not block the E2E suite from running concurrently. Also removes the pnpm version: latest pin in favour of the packageManager field in package.json, adds --frozen-lockfile to prevent silent lockfile mutations in CI, and removes the unused fetch-depth: 2 option from the checkout step.\n\n* ci(publish): split npm and docker publishing into parallel jobs\n\nExtract Release Please output retrieval into a dedicated job and run npm package publishing and Docker image building in parallel, both depending on that shared job. This reduces total publish time when both packages and apps are released together, and separates the two concerns so a failure in one does not block the other.\n\n* chore: add workflow\n\nAdded rollback workflow with placeholder body\n\n* docs(deploy): clarify how to enable manual approval via GitHub Environments\n\nThe existing commented-out environment key lacked any explanation of what it does or how to activate it. Replaced the comment with a full description of what uncommenting the line enables and what must be configured in GitHub first.\n\n* docs(deploy): clarify how to enable manual approval via GitHub Environments\n\nThe existing commented-out environment key lacked any explanation of what it does or how to activate it. Replaced the comment with a full description of what uncommenting the line enables and what must be configured in GitHub first.\n\n* docs(setup): rewrite setup documentation\n\nRewrote setup.md from scratch to cover the full repository configuration required before the release chain is operational. The previous version covered only the GitHub Actions workflow permissions and personal access token for Release Please. The new version adds secrets for npm and Docker Hub publishing, branch protection rules for enforcing the Test workflow as a required status check on main, a table of contents, and consistent section introductions throughout.\n\n* docs: add privately-publishing guide for GitHub Packages and GHCR\n\nDocuments how to switch the Publish workflow from the default public targets — npmjs.com and Docker Hub — to GitHub-hosted alternatives. Covers the package.json changes required for GitHub Packages, including scoped naming and publishConfig, and the workflow changes required for both GitHub Packages and the GitHub Container Registry.\n\n* chore: format\n\n* ci: merge workflows\n\nMerged release + publish + deploy into one workflow\n\n* chore: migrate docs\n\nMigrated docs to docs site\n\n* ci: update rollback workflow\n\nUpdated rollback workflow placeholder body\n\n* ci: add timeout\n\nAdded timeout to build and test jobs\n\n* fix: collapse test workflow into single job\n\n* feat: split workflows\n\nSplit release, publish and deploy into standalone workflows\n\n* fix: configure release-please tag format\n\nConfigured release-please tag format to use component prefix\n\n* chore: add packages/shared to release-please config and manifest\n\n* docs: add publishing guidance to shared package readme\n\n* feat: update rollback workflow\n\nUpdated rollback workflow with run-name and ghcr image\n\n* chore: remove changelog\n\nThe release workflow manages changelogs automatically at the package and app level, so the manual changelog tip is redundant and potentially confusing.\n\n* docs: update tooling\n\nUpdated tooling seciton to cover workflows\n\n* chore: remove docs\n\nRemoved redundant docs\n\n* chore: add .npmrc\n\nAdded .npmrc for GitHub Packages registry support\n\n* ci: add action\n\nAdded a reusable action\n\n* ci: update workflow\n\n* ci: add space between steps\n\nAdded space between steps for improved readability\n\n* chore: updated .npmrc\n\nUpdated .npmrc for improved docs on how to use\n\n* chore: support optional authentication\n\nUpdate the pnpm install step in the Dockerfile to optionally mount an npm_token build secret and append the auth token to .npmrc before installing dependencies. If no secret is provided, install proceeds without authentication and only public packages are resolved. The .npmrc file is removed immediately after install in the same RUN instruction so no credentials are stored in any image layer.\n\n* chore: updated .npmrc\n\nUpdated .npmrc so it reads more naturally with registry first and auth docs second\n\n* chore: add env var\n\nAdded NODE_AUTH_TOKEN in the environment for Docker image builds and update comments for clarity.\n\n* chore: update pnpm install action description and inputs\n\nRefine action description and add optional inputs for registry URL and scope.\n\n* chore: update default registry-url in pnpm install action\n\nSet default registry-url to an empty string for flexibility.\n\n* chore: update .npmrc comments for clarity\n\nClarify instructions for configuring GitHub Packages in .npmrc.\n\n* chore: update deployment image reference in workflows\n\nChange GHCR image name example to use a generic organization format.\n\n* chore: update npm install command in Dockerfile\n\nRefine npm install command to improve clarity and maintain security during build.\n\n* chore: update pnpm install action in workflows\n\nAdd registry-url and scope parameters for GitHub Packages.\n\n* chore: update default node version in pnpm install action\n\nSet the default node version to ''22.20.0'' for consistency.\n\n* chore: update comments for clarity in publish workflow\n\nImprove comments in publish.yml for better understanding of tag processing and Docker image building.\n\n* chore: update publish workflow\n\nEnhance comments and error handling in the publish workflow for better maintainability and debugging.\n\n* chore: update comments for clarity in publish workflow\n\nEnhance comments in publish.yml for better understanding of workflow logic.\n\n* chore: :sparkles: update deployment and rollback workflows\n\nAdd validation for deployment and rollback inputs, and provide template instructions for configuration.\n\n* docs: update GitHub Actions CI/CD description\n\nClarify the role of deploy/rollback workflow templates in the README.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRTrECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA88QQACLN5CnX8vgR36nZv4zEpQ5U\n6/ews+EbtvmNb8NOhB18k/OyRRvn6vFjs9dIrw6rrK2slrtZPZ8cP43UNzoCt/ve\nHXmn1GWwurkp/+tNHfpRd1ZuNR1ieQOCkgs3M8c344gcbUWXd2rwjNwGLtlx7CAs\nh1OdhMHG49QP+MpD6wZzorD7nqMN1hgsa/66xPGEyBCfJijB8NTKImFkZJNhpbG+\nsqVkCtNiTSJFtHEBggiBSkLvaf3WlCMtecOHi94DUrEw2S9yyfgml9zdjonWU8UK\nwwHTfbAX5sLuDUtbEm6mDewGDiZ2NTpDB2HNEeKDnSNEQ/ocR5uZN00wL9XhNIAK\nChfSY+z8Yho81u6xHpwp0OXx0g9RxK