/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andrewdyer/react-vite-turborepo-template/commits/64ca1a3fdf5c49d593e07ac462b7ad0ad6a70461/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-19T12:42:04Z","email":"andrewdyer@outlook.com","name":"Andrew Dyer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-19T12:42:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: add release workflow (#20)\n\n* chore: :wrench: add release workflow\n\nSet up release-please with configuration and manifest for automated releases.\n\n* docs: update contributor guidance for commits and releases\n\nExpand the contribution documentation to define Conventional Commits more clearly, explain how commit types map to semantic version bumps, and add a dedicated release section describing the Release Please workflow from merge to tagged release. This also adds practical guidance on scopes and pull request title formatting so contributors can produce release-compatible history consistently.\n\n* docs: update commit guidelines to include dependency updates\n\nAdd a new commit type ''deps'' to the guidelines, clarifying that dependency updates can trigger a patch release when treated as releasable by Release Please. This change aims to improve clarity for contributors regarding versioning practices.\n\n* docs: add repository Copilot instructions\n\nAdd a dedicated Copilot instructions document that defines the repository’s Conventional Commits requirements, scope rules, and body format so generated commit messages stay consistent and compatible with the Release Please versioning workflow.\n\n* docs: update component usage examples scope\n\nChange the scope in the commit message example from ''ui'' to ''shared'' for clarity.","tree":{"sha":"8d755bac9af8185739eb2aff1373b712f669ce50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andrewdyer/react-vite-turborepo-template/git/trees/8d755bac9af8185739eb2aff1373b712f669ce50"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andrewdyer/react-vite-turborepo-template/git/commits/64ca1a3fdf5c49d593e07ac462b7ad0ad6a70461","verification":{"payload":"tree 8d755bac9af8185739eb2aff1373b712f669ce50\nparent 1206b43071c0baf6f8aa940a9f8c7ed8f05ec622\nauthor Andrew Dyer <andrewdyer@outlook.com> 1781872924 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781872924 +0100\n\nci: add release workflow (#20)\n\n* chore: :wrench: add release workflow\n\nSet up release-please with configuration and manifest for automated releases.\n\n* docs: update contributor guidance for commits and releases\n\nExpand the contribution documentation to define Conventional Commits more clearly, explain how commit types map to semantic version bumps, and add a dedicated release section describing the Release Please workflow from merge to tagged release. This also adds practical guidance on scopes and pull request title formatting so contributors can produce release-compatible history consistently.\n\n* docs: update commit guidelines to include dependency updates\n\nAdd a new commit type ''deps'' to the guidelines, clarifying that dependency updates can trigger a patch release when treated as releasable by Release Please. This change aims to improve clarity for contributors regarding versioning practices.\n\n* docs: add repository Copilot instructions\n\nAdd a dedicated Copilot instructions document that defines the repository’s Conventional Commits requirements, scope rules, and body format so generated commit messages stay consistent and compatible with the Release Please versioning workflow.\n\n* docs: update component usage examples scope\n\nChange the scope in the commit message example from ''ui'' to ''shared'' for clarity.","reason":"va