YzQ5ZDU5M2UwN2FjNDYyYjdhZDBhZDZhNzA0NjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/andrewdyer/react-vite-turborepo-template/commit/1206b43071c0baf6f8aa940a9f8c7ed8f05ec622","sha":"1206b43071c0baf6f8aa940a9f8c7ed8f05ec622","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andrewdyer/react-vite-turborepo-template/commits/1206b43071c0baf6f8aa940a9f8c7ed8f05ec622"}],"sha":"64ca1a3fdf5c49d593e07ac462b7ad0ad6a70461","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andrewdyer/react-vite-turborepo-template/commits/64ca1a3fdf5c49d593e07ac462b7ad0ad6a70461"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8114523?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/andrewdyer","id":8114523,"login":"andrewdyer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTQ1MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewdyer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andrewdyer/react-vite-turborepo-template/commits/1206b43071c0baf6f8aa940a9f8c7ed8f05ec622/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-18T22:46:53Z","email":"andrewdyer@outlook.com","name":"Andrew Dyer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-18T22:46:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: :hammer: update Docker setup and improve Nginx caching strategy (#19)\n\n* chore(docker): remove unused docker-bake.hcl file\n\nDelete docker-bake.hcl as it is no longer needed in the project.\n\n* docs: update Docker section for clarity\n\nClarify Dockerfile usage and remove reference to docker-bake.hcl.\n\n* fix(nginx): :bug: stop caching index.html and scope asset caching to /assets/\n\nPreviously index.html had no explicit cache policy, so a stale cached copy could outlive a deploy and reference hashed asset filenames that no longer exist. Cache-Control: no-cache is now set explicitly on index.html, and long-lived immutable caching is scoped to /assets/ (Vite''s hashed build output) instead of matching on file extension, so a missing asset 404s rather than silently falling back to index.html.\n\nAlso adds gzip for text-based assets and disables the nginx version in response headers.\n\n* chore(dockerfile): :wrench: remove redundant WORKDIR declarations in multi-stage build\n\nRemove duplicate WORKDIR /app statements from the prune and build stages of the Dockerfile. These stages already inherit the working directory from the base image, so the additional declarations were unnecessary no-ops with no functional impact.\n\n* chore(docker): :wrench: update turbo prune syntax to current Turborepo format\n\nUpdate `turbo prune` command to use the current positional argument syntax instead of the deprecated `--scope` flag, aligning with modern Turborepo 2.x behaviour for generating Docker-optimised pruned outputs.\n\n* chore(docker): :wrench: improve layer caching by reordering turbo prune outputs\n\nReorder Docker COPY steps to prioritise `out/json` and lockfile before `out/full`, enabling proper Docker layer caching for `pnpm install`. This ensures dependency installation is only invalidated when the dependency graph changes, rather than on every source code change.\n\n* fix(docker): :bug: correct path for Nginx config copy\n\nUpdate the COPY command for the Nginx server configuration to use the correct relative path.\n\n* fix(nginx): :bug: update index.html caching behavior\n\nEnsure index.html is revalidated with the server to provide fresh asset references after each deploy.","tree":{"sha":"0b9b96a6b32089a90963aaac050e2c1973df8f31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andrewdyer/react-vite-turborepo-template/git/trees/0b9b96a6b32089a90963aaac050e2c1973df8f31"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andrewdyer/react-vite-turborepo-template/git/commits/1206b43071c0baf6f8aa940a9f8c7ed8f05ec622","verification":{"payload":"tree 0b9b96a6b32089a90963aaac050e2c1973df8f31\nparent ee23639d093208016f6a5e38ce7b31a2667c22e0\nauthor Andrew Dyer <andrewdyer@outlook.com> 1781822813 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781822813 +0100\n\nrefactor: :hammer: update Docker setup and improve Nginx caching strategy (#19)\n\n* chore(docker): remove unused docker-bake.hcl file\n\nDelete docker-bake.hcl as it is no longer needed in the project.\n\n* docs: update Docker section for clarity\n\nClarify Dockerfile usage and remove reference to docker-bake.hcl.\n\n* fix(nginx): :bug: stop caching index.html and scope asset caching to /assets/\n\nPreviously index.html had no explicit cache policy, so a stale cached copy could outlive a deploy and reference hashed asset filenames that no longer exist. Cache-Control: no-cache is now set explicitly on index.html, and long-lived immutable caching is scoped to /assets/ (Vite''s hashed build output) instead of matching on file extension, so a missing asset 404s rather than silently falling back to index.html.\n\nAlso adds gzip for text-based assets and disables the nginx version in response headers.\n\n* chore(dockerfile): :wrench: remove redundant WORKDIR declarations in multi-stage build\n\nRemove duplicate WORKDIR /app statements from the prune and build stages of the Dockerfile. These stages already inherit the working directory from the base image, so the additional declarations were unnecessary no-ops with no functional impact.\n\n* chore(docker): :wrench: update turbo prune syntax to current Turborepo format\n\nUpdate `turbo prune` command to use the current positional argument syntax instead of the deprecated `--scope` flag, aligning with modern Turborepo 2.x behaviour for generating Docker-optimised pruned outputs.\n\n* chore(docker): :wrench: improve layer caching by reordering turbo prune outputs\n\nReorder Docker COPY steps to prioritise `out/json` and lockfile before `out/full`, enabling proper Docker layer caching for `pnpm install`. This ensures dependency installation is only invalidated when the dependency graph changes, rather than on every source code change.\n\n* fix(docker): :bug: correct path for Nginx config copy\n\nUpdate the COPY command for the Nginx server configuration to use the correct relative path.\n\n* fix(nginx): :bug: update index.html caching behavior\n\nEnsure index.html is revalidated with the server to provide fresh asset references after each deploy.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNHVdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAePkQAIehF39wF3RQzMOk2C6mZp5V\nMjwuqqRkJvw3EYBe0GRNgfi7AOacRlCmYtJihlDmPrsO+67Pt4d9vuTqcpo3SMh4\nUHckygtv7H9p+Zm+H2EM699iuDP2MTkJOVDJgsDxTvZAbk5bb0BUx0m8/kpUC+Of\nbfrGz+p88bbgbjbKsJ6sYZlDFnP8d6s0HORp25LEO6mJ2DXbZUcOHKBJ2bAFuKk0\n4ST4UkYB2m6iBzAzgF/UoC9qn884YR5HpOktvxnIY33LsXQZzuIR1eWDK8dLVWjD\nLP2WIj9ZWD1ObTvCve96MdplyXHRFH8cTnCwsF4uz/0/s78EOR79jY1KcAQUhSZz\nWXx7fTEnak3OyGDE2rf2atF2vRoSygxC52hrp/hzU5oNA3vfjTpl8CNimnj4S3Yo\n+/IVX5Uh7fI4Vauqo9q9a4UwzLdzSuhJfITwe9DdvZaA/IozdG+Y4z7CKjxiDxuV\nUv/h5GTVFcy6MA2oKXkbxjSfHpLAoBKShIqqfE5inI9QFfcHi5JlMdDTX57UlrqK\n4ONEAmQOTJ9tjul2bhJvwDzVC8+0IM4fv9HaeIvRgYPmhb7JjcXG0bsjz6UoeTLg\nyKdFfp0+XNlgaAJqcV53bgzncGE85F2DilDFY0ZyOngnk0d2Ed6LnUr1VSUj7tI4\ncZpVSOoZ3ZgShOtkuPrB\n=PnZV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-18T22:46:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","