ors.\n\n* docs: :books: update CONTRIBUTING.md to clarify commit guidelines\n\nRevised the commit guidelines section to emphasize the importance of clear commit practices and the use of Conventional Commits format, while removing the redundant \"Submitting Changes\" section.","tree":{"sha":"e25d552e8734e4b66ecdc1139f6097a8fd85ed84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andrewdyer/react-vite-turborepo-template/git/trees/e25d552e8734e4b66ecdc1139f6097a8fd85ed84"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andrewdyer/react-vite-turborepo-template/git/commits/af0f8567af1ac29c56980ee89bf7db58454a0d2f","verification":{"payload":"tree e25d552e8734e4b66ecdc1139f6097a8fd85ed84\nparent fc188e199484777c3a69b73352e7e832e68aac47\nauthor Andrew Dyer <andrewdyer@outlook.com> 1759950164 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1759950164 +0100\n\ndocs: :books: add documentation (#7)\n\n* docs: :books: update README with detailed project structure and features\n\nExpanded the README to include a comprehensive overview of the project structure, tooling, and key features of the applications and packages within the monorepo.\n\n* fix: :bug: correct image formatting in README\n\nUpdated the image section in the README for better clarity and consistency in presentation.\n\n* docs: :books: add Contributor Covenant Code of Conduct\n\nEstablish a Code of Conduct to promote a harassment-free community experience and outline acceptable behavior standards.\n\n* docs: :books: add CONTRIBUTING.md with guidelines for contributors\n\nThis commit introduces a new CONTRIBUTING.md file that outlines the project''s contribution guidelines, including setup instructions, coding standards, commit guidelines, and testing procedures to ensure a smooth contribution experience.\n\n* docs: :books: update README.md\n\nAdded more docs around Turborepo for clarity.\n\n* feat: :sparkles: add issue templates for bug reports, feature requests, and questions\n\nCreated structured templates to streamline issue reporting, 