.com/users/iloveagent57","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edx/frontend-app-learner-portal-enterprise/commits/98790d049153d324d6bf37609f851987bdb98d17/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-06T13:55:02Z","email":"adusenbery@2u.com","name":"Alexander Dusenbery"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-06T14:45:39Z","email":"alex.dusenbery@gmail.com","name":"Alex Dusenbery"},"message":"fix: use resolved Algolia index name in CategoryCard and ai-pathways\n\nCategoryCard was calling algoliasearch().initIndex(ALGOLIA_INDEX_NAME)\ndirectly, bypassing the use_algolia_index_v2 enterprise flag. Switch to\nuseAlgoliaSearch() which already resolves the v2 index name.\n\nusePathways was passing config.ALGOLIA_INDEX_NAME explicitly to\nuseAlgoliaSearch, forcing the v1 index regardless of the flag. Drop the\nargument so the hook resolves the index name itself.\n\nuseCatalogAlgoliaSearch (stage override hook) and catalogFacetService\n(defensive fallback path) were also falling back to ALGOLIA_INDEX_NAME\nwithout checking ALGOLIA_INDEX_NAME_V2 first.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f3d003b8f41857e3bb6edf6d2eb9d388f36b0717","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edx/frontend-app-learner-portal-enterprise/git/trees/f3d003b8f41857e3bb6edf6d2eb9d388f36b0717"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edx/frontend-app-learner-portal-enterprise/git/commits/98790d049153d324d6bf37609f851987bdb98d17","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2307986?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iloveagent57/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iloveagent57/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iloveagent57/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iloveagent57/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":